          "start_ms": null,
          "status": "needs-review",
          "text": "Description: On Saturday, March 2, 2013 at 7 PM, two people were greatly intrigued by the passage over their home of round, slightly flattened, orange glowing objects. The objects appeared in two stages, with a 5-minute interval, and the observation lasted a total of 10 minutes. These objects moved silently from southeast to northeast before disappearing into the altitude. No photographs were taken by the witnesses during their observation. The witness's account: round, flattened, glowing, orange shape, moving alone then in groups of 3, at low altitude (overcast sky), on a Saturday evening, clearly recalls Thai lanterns. The witness's impression of great size is due to the short distance of the objects. The Meteociel report for Lille indicates a variable wind from the northeast to the east, not exactly in line with the objects' movement: the slight relief (Halluin Mountain, 30 meters above the plain) could possibly explain the deviation of the flying objects. These indicators are considered sufficient to classify this case as \"B\": probable observation of the passage of Thai lanterns.",
          "translation_text_sha256": "49d3f3fefd75a72f6e2fa503236d93f77a34b01355a5c9dde4f9e1cb5a329b78"
        }
